A component declared in a platform override body reads and writes that body's
state, the way one declared in an ordinary body does (#230 over #202). An
override *is* the body its target renders, so "the body it was written in" is
well defined and the capture lowering applies to it unchanged.

`inner` names `label` (the base declaration's prop), `count` (the base
declaration's var), `bump()` (the base declaration's method -- the only place
an override body can reach a func, since one written in an override body is
not registered) and `extra` (a var the override body itself declares). It
declares a var of its own, so passInlinePure will not substitute it and the
capture has to survive passNoInlineComponents.

Two overrides rather than one because the two lowering models answer
separately: html patches a static tree, bubbletea re-renders from a model.

What this pins is the ir.Body half. The checker holds the owner link only
while it has the override installed, and pass2 runs after it is restored --
so the nested body is checked while it still holds, and the link itself
travels in the override's own ir.Body for specializeComp to swap back in.
Without it every target emitted the captured names bare: `count = count + 1`,
`state.bump()`, `label + " "`, with nothing declaring any of them.

deny * `\bcount\b` -- the captured var is the owner's, so every target names the per-owner-instance clone and never the declared name
deny * `\bextra\b` -- the var the override body declares is captured the same way and gets the same clone
deny * `\blabel\b` -- the captured prop is substituted by the instantiation's argument, so no target emits its name
deny * `\bbump\b` -- the owner's method is cloned per owner instance, so every target calls the clone and never the declared name
broken out/go/bubbletea -- interpolating an int into a string emits `"L " + m.count__inst2` with no conversion
-- app.sngl --
import . "sngl:ui"
import "sngl:platform/html"
import "sngl:platform/bubbletea"

output {
    none {
        html
    }
    go {
        bubbletea
    }
}

component outer(label = "") node {
    var count = 0

    func bump() { count = count + 100 }

    text(value="base {label} {count}")
}

component outer[html.platform] {
    var extra = 5

    component inner(step = 1) node {
        var runs = 0

        vbox {
            text(value="{label} {count} {extra} {runs}")
            button(text="+", @click {
                count = count + step
                extra = extra + 1
                runs = runs + 1
                bump()
            })
        }
    }

    vbox {
        inner(step=1)
        inner(step=10)
    }
}

component outer[bubbletea.platform] {
    var extra = 5

    component inner(step = 1) node {
        var runs = 0

        vbox {
            text(value="{label} {count} {extra} {runs}")
            button(text="+", @click {
                count = count + step
                extra = extra + 1
                runs = runs + 1
                bump()
            })
        }
    }

    vbox {
        inner(step=1)
        inner(step=10)
    }
}

window {
    outer(label="L")
}
